When generating a Git commit message for this repository, follow these rules exactly.

- Write one subject line only. Do not add a body.
- Format: `type: message`
- The type is lowercase. Put exactly one space after the colon.
- The message is Korean and briefly says why the change was made.
- Allowed types only:
  - feat: a user-visible feature
  - chor: config, dependencies, or build work that is not a feature
  - fix: a bug fix
  - refactor: a structure change that keeps the same behavior
  - docs: documentation
  - style: formatting or visual style
  - test: tests
- Do not use `Feat:`, `feat(scope):`, `chore:`, or an English subject.

Examples:
feat: 테마와 언어 설정을 저장해 다시 열어도 유지되게 함
chor: TypeScript 6에서 폐기된 baseUrl 설정을 제거함
fix: 새로고침 때 저장된 테마가 깜빡이지 않게 함
